Embedded tree-sitter WebAssembly modules
========================================

Each <language>.wasm in this directory is one wasm32-wasi reactor module that contains:

  - the tree-sitter core library        MIT            LICENSES/tree-sitter.txt
  - one tree-sitter grammar             see its file   LICENSES/<language>.txt
  - diffduck's shim (../shim/shim.c)    this repository's licence
  - wasi-libc, linked in by zig         Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT,
                                        with musl (MIT), dlmalloc (CC0), and cloudlibc
                                        (BSD-2-Clause) portions   LICENSES/wasi-libc.txt

The tree-sitter core includes src/portable/endian.h by Mathias Panzenböck, placed in the public
domain (or, where that is not possible, under BSD, MIT, or Apache licences at your option).

Provenance
----------

Nothing here is downloaded as a binary. scripts/build-treesitter-wasm.sh compiles every module
from source:

  - core:     github.com/tree-sitter/go-tree-sitter at the version pinned in the script (its
              src/ and include/ are the official tree-sitter C library),
  - grammars: the module and version pinned in scripts/treesitter/<language>.env,

both fetched through the Go module proxy, so sum.golang.org verifies their contents. The
compiler is zig 0.13.0 (pinned; the --docker mode installs the official release tarball and
checks its sha256). The same inputs produce byte-identical modules.

Rebuild one language with `make treesitter-wasm GRAMMAR=python`, or all with
`make treesitter-wasm`.

typescript.wasm and tsx.wasm are the two dialects of one grammar module, tree-sitter-typescript;
LICENSES/typescript.txt and LICENSES/tsx.txt hold its one licence.
